**Resolution:** Agent informed the customer that **5 advance EMIs** had already been paid. The agent explained that when an EMI is paid in advance within the same month, the payment is treated as a **part-payment** and is adjusted towards the **outstanding principal amount**. As a result, the first advance EMI was adjusted against the outstanding principal and the last EMI of the loan schedule, which is why the system was showing an EMI bounce status.

